"Boe, sometimes written Bo, is Alden Thorn's longest friend, since middle school."
"He is the mean one of the group, scathing, and sixteen years old."
"He wears horn-rimmed glasses, a grandmotherly knitted scarf and a bowl haircut."
"He also wears an even uglier knitted hat."
"A Bedlam Beldam poster has hung over his bed since he was eight."
"He once had an epic superhero obsession and knows some superhuman politics."
"His parents are chronically checked out; by twelve he did the cooking and cleaning."
"He is loyal, sarcastic and funny, bad at new friends, by turns robotic and ill-tempered."
"His GPA is bloated by advanced classes, to 5.3 on a 4.0 scale."
"He rants about self-made mononyms, such as the Chicago hero Sharon's."
"He likes puzzles and anagrams."
"He suspects phone calls are scanned for keywords."
"He suggested Alden stay unregistered and become an elementary school teacher."
"He looked nearly devastated for a moment when Alden chose to be a hero."
"He disguised Alden from Skiff with his own hat and scarf."
"He found out that Let Me Take Your Luggage is a Rabbit skill."
"He takes consulate classes with Jeremy and records the Artonan Life lecture for Alden."
"He cooks breakfast hash with tofu and coconut bacon."
"He keeps a binder of skill tests for Alden."
"He knows Alden's phone passcode and covers for Alden with Aunt Connie."
"While Alden is summoned he keeps Alden's phone, feeds Victor and handles school for him."
"He says the System is obviously spying on everyone."
"He researched Manon's social media and college paper and thinks her friendly act is fake."
"He declared Alden dead the same day the Artonans listed him missing."
"After Alden's memorial he ran away for over a week, then punched a hole in Jeremy's wall."
"He did not return to school after Alden's disappearance."
"By Alden's CNH assessment he had sent Alden no word for nearly two months."
"He was secretly selected before Alden vanished: an A-rank U-type, a Sway and Mourner blended."
"He never accepted the Contract; the System offers it each morning two minutes after he wakes."
"His skill Kitty Moon Barrier, named for Bedlam Beldam, blocks others' emotions from him."
"His second skill magnifies emotions or forces his own onto people, dangerous to both sides."
"His skill I Need a Break from People sends him to catspace, then out beside an attached host."
"Attached to Victor, he reappeared naked in Alden's apartment on Anesidora."
"Unshielded he is an empathic sponge, sensing people about two apartments in every direction."
"He is more durable than strong; punching through Jeremy's brick wall was his maximum effort."
"He strictly limits how many people he lets himself care about."
"He hid in Alden's apartment until leaving the island, vowing to save nine lives to match Alden."
"He calls himself a Scumbag Type hero and urges Alden to stop wishing he were Hannah."
"His dream is to buy a shabby boat, live alone just offshore and earn degrees online."
"His new hero type is copying Alden's moral lead: partners in heroics, long distance."
"Alden gave him blanket permission to read Alden's emotions."
"Alden sent him about two million Argold for survival, summons emergencies and escape plans."
"He read Gorgon on purpose and found very alien emotions, including anguish when Alden vanished."
"In November he left Anesidora in catspace inside Victor, who teleported to Jeremy in Chicago."
"His public cover story is that he ran away after Alden's funeral and will return."
